\id GEN
\c 2
\p
\v 21 So the \nd Lord\nd* God caused a deep sleep to fall upon the man, and he slept; and He took one of his ribs\f + \ft Or sides\f* and closed up the area with flesh.
\v 22 And from the rib the \nd Lord\nd* God had taken from the man, He made a woman and brought her to the man.
\v 23 And the man said:
\q1 “This is now bone of my bones
\q2 and flesh of my flesh;
\q1 she shall be called ‘woman,’
\q2 for out of man she was taken.”
\p
\v 24 For this reason a man shall leave his father and his mother and hold fast to his wife, and they shall become one flesh.\f + \ft Cited in Matthew 19:5\f*
